  "title": "oampdu: give the dgt_set_t a better name.",
  "description": "The name was Dgt1_9_bcd but, in fact, it supports digits 0-9, not 1-9.\n\nThat's used for a YYYY/MM/DD date, which *obviously* requires zeros, so\nno way is it 1-9 - two weeks from today is 2023/10/10!\n\nAgain, the renaming makes it clearer that this these fields could use\nproto_tree_add_item() with the encoding\nENC_BCD_DIGITS_0_9|ENC_BIG_ENDIAN (and neither ENC_BCD_SKIP_FIRST nor\nENC_BCD_ODD_NUM_DIG) if the encodings there could support both\nbig-endian and little-endian digit order within a byte (see !12239).",
